patch.description:
Update several labelled elements in a single request.  Each key in the `fields` object is a label name.

Values can be:
- A **string** — shorthand to update only the text content
- An **object** — full style update (same shape as the PATCH single-field body)

**Example:**
```json
{
  "fields": {
    "headline": "Breaking News",
    "price": {"content": "$9.99", "color": "#00ff00", "fontSize": 48},
    "bg_panel": {"backgroundColor": "#1a1a2e", "opacity": 0.9}
  }
}
```

Returns a list of results per label.  Labels that don't exist are reported in a `not_found` entry rather than causing a 404.

props.description:
Type-specific visual properties. Shape depends on `type`:
• **text**: {content, fontSize, fontFamily, fontWeight, color, backgroundColor, align, lineHeight}
• **panel**: {backgroundColor, borderRadius, borderColor, borderWidth, opacity}
• **image**: {contentId, objectFit}
• **video**: {contentId, muted, loop, objectFit}
